  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nShowers and storms will kick off today, particularly across western \nzones, from a combination of heating, and a disturbance that will \nmove into the area. Isolated severe storms are possible, due to the \noverall moderate to strong cape, and anomalously high PW content air \nin place, with the potential for downburst winds to occur. SPC has \nadded far western/southern zones into a marginal risk for severe. \n\nLight steering flow, along with the anomalously high water content \nin the atmosphere, will result in the potential for localized \nflooding issues for today. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nAdditional showers and storms are expected on Saturday, with the \npotential for more widespread severe. An upper trough, with multiple \nshortwaves, will affect the area on Saturday, with a surface cold \nfront sweeping across the area Saturday night into Sunday, with some \ndrier air working in, at least across the north for Sunday. \nStrengthening flow, combined with ample instability will result in \nthe potential for severe storms, with damaging winds the primary \nhazard, although there is a small potential for a tornado, mainly \nacross far northern zones with low LCL heights expected and marginal \n0-1km SRH. There does exist some concern with evolution of severe \ndepending on any morning convection/lingering clouds and its affects \non the atmosphere, but confidence in limiting affects on severe is \nrather low at this point. There also exists the potential for \nisolated water issues on Saturday. Storms should generally move \nalong well, but with heavy rain rates anticipated, localized flash \nflooding is a concern. \n\nIn addition, the storms, along with increased flow should result in \nsome improvement to the wildfire smoke and air quality issues \nobserved across the area.",
